<%# PronounceAll — Copyright (C) 2026 Alp Kavaklı
    SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
    See LICENSE-NOTICE.md at the repository root.

    The phoneme learning pages (FR-IPA-07, FR-IPA-10).

    One template, two scopes. The per-variant page lists one variant's
    inventory; the global page lists every active variant's and shows a variant
    marker on each row, which is the only rendering difference between them
    (FR-IPA-10).

    Uncached and DYNAMIC. SDD §6.3 names the learning pages among the responses
    B2 does NOT make cacheable, because FR-IPA-07 gives each row a per-viewer
    save state. There is still no inline script or style here.

    PARTIALLY SATISFIED, deliberately, and on the rule this project has applied
    throughout — a control that cannot work is worse than none:

      * the play-audio button of FR-IPA-07/FR-IPA-10 renders only where a READY
        asset backs it. Every phoneme asset is currently `pending`, so no button
        appears yet;
      * the save/tag control of §4.3 is Iteration 3 and is absent.

    The ranked inventory, the symbols, and the FR-IPA-08 sound-matched examples
    are all here and correct. %>
<!doctype html>
<html lang="<%= scope === 'variant' ? variant.code : 'en' %>">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head', { title: title }) %>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="page learn-ipa">
    <h1><%= scope === 'variant' ? `The sounds of ${variant.displayName}` : 'The sounds of every language' %></h1>

    <p class="lede">
      <%= phonemes.length %> teaching units, most common first. Every English
      word is built from these.
    </p>

    <% if (scope === 'variant') { %>
      <%- include('partials/search-form', { variantCode: variant.code }) %>
    <% } %>

    <% if (phonemes.length === 0) { %>
      <p class="search__hint">No phonemes have been seeded yet.</p>
    <% } else { %>
      <%# FR-IPA-07: ordered by ascending frequency rank, which is the order the
          query returned. Nothing re-sorts it here. %>
      <ol class="phoneme-list">
        <% phonemes.forEach(function (phoneme) { %>
          <li class="phoneme-row">
            <span class="phoneme-row__rank" aria-hidden="true"><%= phoneme.frequencyRank %></span>

            <span class="phoneme-row__symbol" lang="und-fonipa">
              <span class="visually-hidden">Phoneme: </span><%= phoneme.ipaSymbol %>
            </span>

            <span class="phoneme-row__example">
              <% if (phoneme.exampleWord) { %>
                as in <strong><%= phoneme.exampleWord %></strong>
                <% if (phoneme.examplePhonemicTranscription) { %>
                  <span class="phoneme-row__example-ipa" lang="und-fonipa">/<%= phoneme.examplePhonemicTranscription %>/</span>
                <% } %>
              <% } %>
            </span>

            <% if (scope === 'global') { %>
              <%# FR-IPA-10: the marker identifying which variant the phoneme
                  belongs to. Only the global page shows it — on the per-variant
                  page every row would carry the same value. %>
              <span class="phoneme-row__variant"><%= phoneme.variantCode %></span>
            <% } %>

            <%# FR-IPA-07/10 list a play-audio button. It appears once a real
                asset exists; until then there is nothing to play and no button. %>
            <% if (phoneme.hasAudio) { %>
              <audio class="phoneme-row__audio" controls preload="none"
                     src="<%= audioPublicPrefix %>/<%= phoneme.audioStorageKey %>">
                Your browser cannot play this recording.
              </audio>
            <% } %>
          </li>
        <% }); %>
      </ol>
    <% } %>

    <%# FR-CONTENT-05 and NFR-LEGAL-05: the example words are quoted from
        Wiktionary and carry its licence. %>
    <footer class="attribution">
      <p>
        Example words from
        <a href="https://en.wiktionary.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wiktionary</a>
        · CC BY-SA 4.0
      </p>
    </footer>
  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
  <script type="module" src="/js/bootstrap.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
